<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ronnie Brunswijk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1961">1961</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ronnie Brunswijk is a Surinamese Maroon leader and politician, a former soldier and bodyguard of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desi-bouterse">Desi Bouterse</a> who in 1986 founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jungle-commando">Jungle Commando</a> and led it in the interior war against the military regime until 1992. He later founded the General Liberation and Development Party, became a businessman in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a> and served as vice-president of Suriname from 2020 to 2025.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ronnie-brunswijk.jpg" alt="Ronnie Brunswijk" width="320" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ATV-Networks Suriname · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ronnie_Brunswijk_ingezworen.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
